```dafny
method BinarySearch(a: seq<real>, x: real) returns (k: int)
  requires |a| > 0
  requires forall i, j :: 0 <= i < j < |a| ==> a[i] >= a[j]  // a is non-increasing
  ensures 0 <= k <= |a|
  ensures forall i :: 0 <= i < k ==> a[i] >= x
  ensures forall i :: k <= i < |a| ==> a[i] < x
  decreases |a|
{
  if |a| == 1 {
    if a[0] >= x {
      k := 1;
    } else {
      k := 0;
    }
    return;
  }

  var mid := |a| / 2;
  if a[mid] >= x {
    // x belongs in right half including mid
    var right := a[mid..];
    var kRight := BinarySearch(right, x);
    k := mid + kRight;
  } else {
    // x belongs in left half (before mid)
    var left := a[..mid];
    var kLeft := BinarySearch(left, x);
    k := kLeft;
  }
}

// Alternative iterative version
method BinarySearchIterative(a: seq<real>, x: real) returns (k: int)
  requires |a| > 0
  requires forall i, j :: 0 <= i < j < |a| ==> a[i] >= a[j]  // a is non-increasing
  ensures 0 <= k <= |a|
  ensures forall i :: 0 <= i < k ==> a[i] >= x
  ensures forall i :: k <= i < |a| ==> a[i] < x
{
  var low := 0;
  var high := |a|;

  while low < high
    invariant 0 <= low <= high <= |a|
    invariant forall i :: 0 <= i < low ==> a[i] >= x
    invariant forall i :: high <= i < |a| ==> a[i] < x
  {
    var mid := low + (high - low) / 2;
    if a[mid] >= x {
      low := mid + 1;
    } else {
      high := mid;
    }
  }

  k := low;
}

// Helper lemma for verification
lemma BinarySearchLemma(a: seq<real>, x: real, k: int)
  requires |a| > 0
  requires forall i, j :: 0 <= i < j < |a| ==> a[i] >= a[j]
  requires 0 <= k <= |a|
  requires forall i :: 0 <= i < k ==> a[i] >= x
  requires forall i :: k <= i < |a| ==> a[i] < x
  ensures (k == |a| ==> forall i :: 0 <= i < |a| ==> a[i] >= x)
  ensures (k == 0 ==> forall i :: 0 <= i < |a| ==> a[i] < x)
{
  // This lemma helps verify the boundary conditions
  if k == |a| {
    assert forall i :: 0 <= i < |a| ==> a[i] >= x;
  } else if k == 0 {
    assert forall i :: 0 <= i < |a| ==> a[i] < x;
  }
}
```

Key corrections made:

1. **Fixed syntax errors**: Removed incorrect `uses precondition` statements and replaced them with proper `requires` clauses.

2. **Corrected algorithm logic**:
   - The recursive version properly splits the array and adjusts indices
   - The iterative version uses standard binary search loop invariants

3. **Proper preconditions**:
   - Sequence must be non-empty (`|a| > 0`)
   - Sequence must be sorted in non-increasing order (for binary search to work)

4. **Proper postconditions**:
   - `k` is between 0 and `|a|`
   - All elements before index `k` are >= x
   - All elements from index `k` onward are < x

5. **Added termination measures**: Both methods properly decrease the problem size to ensure termination.

6. **Added helper lemma**: To help verify boundary conditions of the search result.

The algorithm finds the first index `k` where `a[k] < x`, assuming the array is sorted in non-increasing order. This is equivalent to finding the insertion point for `x` in a sorted array.
